{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation plan (worktree xenops-fold-race, based on Gerrit 1771 PS2 for doctor shapes; will push WIP until 1771 merges):\n\n1. compact_txn.py — absorbing re-fold semantics: a new fold-input partition helper identifies the latest LIVE snapshot among candidates and its source_event_uuids. (a) When the snapshot itself folds, the reducer's event_files_override is ORDERED as [pre-snapshot cited files, snapshot, orphans by ts, post-snapshot files] so an orphan (pre-snapshot ts, uuid not cited) replays ON TOP of the snapshot — pinned semantics: snapshot, then orphans by ts, then post-snapshot events. The new snapshot cites the orphan uuids, clearing ORPHAN_EVENT. (b) SAFETY GUARD discovered during design: if the live snapshot is within the horizon (young) while pre-snapshot files are foldable, folding those pre-snapshot files ALONE would write a new pre-snapshot SNAPSHOT that the governing snapshot then positionally skips — silently burying the orphan for good. Such pre-snapshot candidates are DEFERRED from the fold until the snapshot itself is foldable. (c) Retired files are never candidates and a live file cited in source_event_uuids is never re-absorbed (replay skips it by uuid; it is re-cited, not re-applied).\n\n2. compact.py — new --absorb-orphans flag: bypasses ONLY the \"remote SNAPSHOT exists\" refusal (which stays for plain rebar compact); sync-before-compact still runs.\n\n3. doctor.py (on 1771 shapes) — read-only scan_orphans() emits ORPHAN_EVENT findings (per ticket, path list); doctor --repair routes them AFTER dirty-tracker repair: reuse 1771's _dirty_backup_ref (refs/rebar-doctor/<utc-ts>) before mutation — no backup ref, no mutation — then per-ticket absorbing re-fold via compact_cli([tid, --threshold=0, --horizon=0, --absorb-orphans]); compact takes the store write lock itself (run_repair holds none, same as the dirty path).\n\nTDD: oracle tests first (race reproduction: fold with the late comment file absent, then materialize it as the union merge would; assert show misses it + ORPHAN_EVENT flagged; then repair => visible + clean), ordering pin (orphan appends after snapshot-absorbed comments, before post-snapshot ones), defer guard, refusal-stays guard, no-reabsorption guards, doctor backup-ref + no-backup-no-mutation. Then implement to green; manual mutation pass targeting absorb-flag inversion, skipped backup ref, dropped source_event_uuids check, ordering swap, retired re-absorption."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786723337518313001,"uuid":"eedd05e9-3663-4e2e-b5a6-ca46d79f0430"}